  "about": "Old MacDonald Had a Farm is a children's song about a farmer and his animals. An early form called \"Ohio\" was printed in 1917, in a book of songs sung by British soldiers. Each verse adds an animal and its sound, so the song lasts as long as the singers like.",
  "funFact": "In the 1917 song the farmer was called Old Macdougal, and his farm was in Ohio.",
